// CLAIM: The editor does not show BMX's four lint warnings, and that is a boundary rather than a gap
// HOLDS: absent
// TERMS: W001 W002 W003 W005 bmx_lint
// WHY: **the probe is an absence because the decision is an absence.** star does not implement BMX's
//      lint rules, and the way that claim goes stale is not by the warnings reappearing — it is by
//      somebody reimplementing the four rules here, one afternoon, to close a gap that is not a gap.
//      This fires the moment one of those codes is declared in this repository.
//
//      An `absent` probe rather than a `refused` one for the same reason
//      `nothing-runs-outside-the-document.absent` is: "there is no X at all" cannot be probed by
//      writing one X. And prose mentioning a code is fine, which is the distinction that keeps this
//      gate from firing on its own explanation — `docs/not-done.md` names the family and must be
//      allowed to.
//
//      The other half is checked where it can be: the server announces on startup that BMX's lint is
//      unavailable, and `editors/lsp/drive-lsp.bx` asserts that it says so. **A capability lost
//      silently is the failure; announced and asserted is the holding position.** So this claim has
//      two guards and neither is prose: nothing may declare the rules, and the server must keep
//      saying they are missing.
//
//      When BMX adds `bmx_lint` to its own public surface — its call, not ours, because it touches a
//      compatibility promise and the format's conformance boundary — the warnings return with no
//      change here, and this probe and its claim go away together.
